  "body": "## What changed\n- **Float noise at the leave limit** (the root cause of the red heavy test `adaptive_plans_the_developed_levels_under_the_load_and_kink_laws`). On the r7 bar the wrap's ladder level comes out as 6.500000000000001, one ulp above the leave limit `air_above` = 6.5. `pocket3d_air_split` split with a bare `>`, so it sorted that level as an air level (one lap) and the plan read 19.9 % D against the 19.7 % law. The new `machining3d::entry::air_levels` counts a plane within `EPS` of the limit as a material plane, as the function's doc already said (\"at or below\"). `pocket3d_air_split` is only called by the rotary wrap.\n- **Narrowed helix refused by name before planning.** On the wrap only (seam present), `hsm::plan_level` now asks the planner's own entry rule (`machining2d::choose_entry`, now `pub(crate)`). If that rule would narrow the requested helix, Offset rings cut the level, with a note: `adaptive: the developed level is too narrow for the helix entry (radius 1.000 asked, 0.900 fits with room to spiral out) - Offset rings cut ... instead`. The note text is exported as `machining3d::NARROW_HELIX`. Before, the narrowed spiral overloaded (15.7 % D).\n- **r6.2 travel refusal: kept and recorded as final.** The 5.7 and 5.2 levels are ~78 × 7.8 and ~78 × 5.8 mm bands round the neck. The variant with lifted returns breaks the planner's own 47.5 deg bound (48.0), and the plain spiral travels 3.2× and 3.9× its cut length out of cut (budget 1.5×). Refusing by name, and cutting with Offset rings, is the safe answer. Planning thin bands properly belongs to #44 and #47. Pinned by name.\n- `rotary_adaptive.rs` (474 lines) is split: fixtures and the level reader move to `crates/motion/tests/rotary_adaptive_fixture/mod.rs`, a module with no binary of its own.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/55-rotary-adaptive-levels.md`.\n\n## Readings (release; D6 ball, leave 0.5, helix r1, limit 19.7 % D)\n| Case | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| r7 bar, radius 6.5 | 19.9 % D (red) | 19.5 % D, two laps |\n| r7 bar, radius 6.0 / 5.5 | 19.5 / 18.8 % | unchanged |\n| r7 bar, posted world program | - | 160,989 moves, 0 in-cut breaks > 5 deg |\n| 10 mm window, stepdown 2 | helix narrowed to 0.9, then 15.7 % overload; radius 5.0 refused after 197 revolutions | both levels refused by name, 0.4 s debug |\n| r6.2 bar, radius 5.7 / 5.2 | refused for travel (8,208 / 8,828 mm out of cut) | still refused, now pinned by name |\n\nThe load margin on the r7 bar is still thin (19.5 against 19.7).\n\n## Posted output\nThis changes posted G-code for **rotary-wrap programs only**: a wrap level at the leave limit is cleared over two laps (as in round 2), and an Adaptive wrap level too narrow for the helix is cut by Offset rings. Planar 2D and 3D pockets are unaffected. The OffsetRings golden digest on the r6.2 bar is unchanged. The PR stays a **draft** for a PathPilot Hub run.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `rotary_adaptive::a_window_too_narrow_for_the_helix_is_refused_by_name_before_planning` (debug)\n- `rotary_adaptive::the_r62_neck_levels_are_refused_for_travel_by_name` (heavy lane)\n- `rotary_adaptive::adaptive_plans_the_developed_levels_under_the_load_and_kink_laws` (heavy lane, red on main, green here)\n- `machining3d::hsm::tests::a_band_too_narrow_for_the_helix_is_named_before_planning`\n- `machining3d::tests::a_plane_at_the_leave_envelope_is_a_material_plane`\n\n## Gate\n- Quick gate on the merge with upstream/main: motion suites green except the known `swarf_pose_continuity` (#351).\n- Worker runs: release `rotary_adaptive --ignored` 4/4, motion lib 151, the rotary and pocket motion suites, and the app rotary suites, all green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nChangelog: Rotary Adaptive: the level at the part's leave limit is no longer sorted by float noise, and a developed band too narrow for the helix entry is cut by Offset rings with a note naming it instead of an overloaded plan (#55)\n\nFixes #55\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
